    <span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Rentals</span>
    <h1>Hanoi Motorbike Rental: Short Riders Pickup Planning</h1>
    <p>Pickup day is the moment a rental stops being a plan and becomes a machine in your hands, and a short rider should plan it as carefully as any other part of a Hanoi trip. The counter sits at 112 Nguyen Van Cu in Long Bien, it opens from 09:00 to 21:00 every day, and the visit deserves an unhurried hour: arriving calm leaves time for the flat-foot test, the paperwork questions, and the first slow lap of the neighborhood.</p>
    <p>This page belongs to the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> cluster and covers pickup planning specifically for shorter riders. Verified prices for every model are on the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">cost hub</a>, general questions live on the <a href="/faq/">FAQ</a> page, and the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/new-riders-pickup-planning/">new riders pickup planning guide</a> treats the same visit for riders new to motorbikes altogether.</p>
    <nav class="toc" aria-label="Table of contents">
      <p>On this page</p>
      <ol>
        <li><a href="#sec-1">Timing the visit to the Long Bien counter</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-2">What to bring and what to leave</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-3">The first ten minutes: fit before paperwork</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-4">A calm first lap of the neighborhood</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-5">Planning around Hanoi traffic windows</a></li>
